    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d437">

                <pb facs="0537" n="442" xml:id="pg442"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/13804: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-12-21T16:00:00+08:00">December 21, 1936—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received December 21—9:04 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>368. Shanghai’s telegram of December 20, 4 p.m., especially paragraph 5.<anchor
                        n="17" xml:id="d437-f1"/></p>
                <p>At my request Dr. Kung undertook on December 19 to send a telegram to Donald as
                    from me asking if latter could make arrangements with the Young Marshal for
                    evacuating American missionaries at Sian. I suggested that this be effected by
                    airplane if possible and that other foreigners be included in the
                    arrangement.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Peiping, Shanghai, Hankow.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
